<BaseLayout title="Acupressure for Neck Pain: Best Points for Fast Relief" description="Learn how to use acupressure for neck pain relief. Guide to GB21, GB20, LI4, and other points that release neck tension and restore mobility." breadcrumbs={[{ "label": "Home", "href": "/" }, { "label": "Conditions", "href": "/conditions/" }, { "label": "Acupressure for Neck Pain: Best Points for Fast Relief", "href": "/conditions/acupressure-for-neck-pain/" }]}>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6"><h1 class="mb-4">Acupressure for Neck Pain: Best Points for Fast Relief</h1><p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-lg mb-8">Neck pain responds exceptionally well to acupressure because many key points are located in the very muscles and meridians that become tense and painful.</p><section id="gb21" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">1. GB21 (Jianjing) - Shoulder Well</h2><p class="mb-3">GB21 is the most important point for neck and shoulder tension. It releases the trapezius muscle, which is often the primary source of neck pain.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Location:</strong> At the highest point of the shoulder, midway between the neck and the shoulder joint.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Technique:</strong> Use your opposite hand to press deeply into the shoulder muscle. Hold for 1-2 minutes while slowly turning your head side to side.</p></section><section id="gb20" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">2. GB20 (Fengchi) - Wind Pool</h2><p class="mb-3">GB20 releases tension at the base of the skull and upper neck, where many people hold stress. <a href="/points/gb20-fengchi-acupressure-point/">GB20 guide</a>.</p></section><section id="si3" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">3. SI3 (Houxi) - Back Ravine</h2><p class="mb-3">SI3 is a specific point for neck pain that also treats acute neck stiffness (wry neck).</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Location:</strong> On the side of the hand, at the end of the pinky finger crease when the hand is in a loose fist.</p></section><section id="li4" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">4. LI4 (Hegu) - Joining Valley</h2><p class="mb-3">LI4 is a distal point that effectively treats pain anywhere in the head and neck area. <a href="/points/li4-hegu-acupressure-point/">LI4 guide</a>.</p></section><section id="routine" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Neck Pain Relief Routine</h2><ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300"><li>Press GB21 on both shoulders for 2 minutes each</li><li>Stimulate GB20 at the skull base for 2 minutes</li><li>Press SI3 on both hands for 1 minute each</li><li>Finish with LI4 on both hands for 1 minute each</li><li>Gently stretch neck by tilting ear toward each shoulder</li></ol></section><section id="evidence" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Scientific Evidence</h2><p class="mb-3">A 2023 study in the Journal of Physical Therapy Science found that acupressure combined with neck stretching reduced chronic neck pain by 60% and improved range of motion significantly within 4 weeks.</p></section><hr class="my-8"><div class="bg-stone-100 dark:bg-stone-800 rounded-lg p-6 text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400"><p><strong>Medical Disclaimer:</strong> Consult a healthcare provider for neck pain following trauma, accompanied by numbness/tingling in arms, or persistent despite self-care.</p></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
